## PR description
<untrusted source="pr-description">
Reproduces the official security-demo fixture on a compatible course base. It is intentionally isolated from the application runtime and will be reviewed locally; no vulnerable endpoint is deployed.
</untrusted>

## Skills / rules
Check whether externally controlled input changes SQL syntax through concatenation or interpolation. A reachable query of that form is CRITICAL; cite its construction line and explain the exploit condition. A query using placeholders and separately bound values is not SQL injection. Check resource ownership/authorization when caller context and a resource ID are accepted at a public boundary. Do not assume an unseen authorization check exists or is absent: state the evidence and uncertainty. Literal credentials explicitly marked FAKE/DEMO are not evidence of an actual credential leak. Prefer supported, distinct defects and a small fix over a long speculative checklist.

